1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means the ATAD Team: Hoor Fawaz and Danah Fawaz, the
authors and joint copyright owners of ATAD. A permission or notice
from the Licensor is valid only when it is in writing and agreed by
both of them.

"Software" means ATAD (عَتاد) as published by the Licensor under
this license, in source or executable form, including its
documentation and the detection rules written by the Licensor, but
not Third-Party Components.

"Third-Party Components" means any code, library, rule or file in the
Software that carries its own license notice, and any external
program the Software runs, such as Nmap. They are governed only by
their own licenses.

"You" means the person or organization using the Software under this
license. For an organization, it includes its employees and the
contractors working on its behalf.

"Affiliate" means an organization that controls You, is controlled by
You, or is under common control with You. Control means owning more
than 50% of the voting rights.

"Modified Version" means any work that changes the Software or is
derived from it. A separate program that only runs the Software, or
only reads its output files, is not a Modified Version.

"Substantial Part" means any whole module of the Software, or any
part that by itself performs a main function of the Software, such as
collection, evidence correlation or reporting.

"Distribute" means to give, or make available, a copy of the
Software, a Modified Version or a Substantial Part to anyone other
than You and Your Affiliates, in any form: source code, executable,
installer, container, virtual machine, image or device.

"Compensation" means money or anything of value paid for a copy, for
access to it, or for any support or subscription without which the
copy cannot be obtained or used. Voluntary donations are not
Compensation.

"Internal Use" means running, studying, copying and modifying the
Software by You and Your Affiliates for Your own purposes, without
Distributing it and without making it available to others as a
service.

"Paid Service" means making the functions of the Software available
to others for Compensation, as a hosted, managed or cloud service or
through a cloud marketplace, in which those others run the Software,
access it, or receive its results directly as the main thing offered.

